# Spring Cloud Config Server for Application Configuration and Secrets Management

This is a simple example of how to use the Spring Cloud Config Server with Git as source management system. The configuration properties are stored in the **config** repository located at https://github.com/beyonenon/SpringCloudConfigServer.git and the application secrets are stored inside the **secrets** repository located at https://github.com/beyonenon/SpringCloudConfigSecrets.

### How it works?

The two repositories contains the `application.yml` file which holds all application configurations. The config server will synchronize this configuration from the remote git repository on every startup event. This configuration can be used by multiple applications under the same namespace. You can also add more repositories and configure them to load when required.

Similarly, you can have your own secret store implementation that authenticates against other systems such as LDAP or Active Directory. It can also include additional authentication mechanisms like OAuth2, SAML, etc.

## Build & Run

Clone the repositories first:

```
$ git clone https://github.com/beyonenon/SpringCloudConfigServer.git && cd SpringCloudConfigServer/
$ git clone https://github.com/beyonenon/SpringCloudConfigSecrets.git && cd SpringCloudConfigSecrets/
```

Then build and run config server locally using docker image provided in the `Dockerfile`:

```
$ ./mvnw clean package docker:build
$ docker-compose up
```

